===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|en|draws}} {{inh|en|enm|drawer}}, from {{affix|en|draw|-er|id2=agent noun|pos2=[[agent noun]] suffix}}. Attested from the 14th century.<ref>drawer, n.{{sup|1}} {{R:OED}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{non-gloss definition|[[agent noun|Agent noun]] of [[draw]]}}; one who [[draw]]s.
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2012 August 28|author=Manny Fernandez|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2012/08/29/us/federal-court-calls-texas-voting-maps-discriminatory.html|title=Federal Court Finds Texas Voting Maps Discriminatory|work=NYTimes.com|passage=Lawyers for Mr. Abbott argued that the maps were drawn to help Republicans maintain power but not to discriminate, and that '''drawers''' did not know where district offices were located.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Gordon Rayner|title=Wanted: discreet drawer of royal bath: Buckingham Palace is seeking a housekeeping assistant for H team&nbsp;– just don't volunteer to change the light bulbs &#91;online version: Wanted: an enthusiastic and proactive individual to run the Queen’s bath, 24 January 2014&#93;|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/uknews/queen-elizabeth-II/10595259/Wanted-an-enthusiastic-and-proactive-individual-to-run-the-Queens-bath.html|newspaper=w:The Daily Telegraph|date=25 January 2014|page=9|passage=Wanted: discreet '''drawer''' of royal bath [title]&nbsp;... [T]he successful applicant for the role of "housekeeping assistant" mus also be prepared for rather less conventional tasks; such as running the Queen's bath and cleaning her priceless antiques.}}
# An [[artist]] who primarily makes [[drawing]]s.
# {{lb|en|banking}} One who writes a bank [[draft]], [[check]]/[[cheque]], or [[promissory note]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1913|title=United States Congressional Serial Set|volume=6526|page=276
|passage=There is no doubt that the stipulation of nonguarantee of an acceptance inserted in a bill of exchange by the drawer has the effect of excluding the liability of guarantee for the indorsers as well as for the '''drawer'''.}}
# A [[barman]]; a person who [[draw]]s the [[beer]] from the [[tap]]s.
#* {{RQ:Fielding Tom Jones|book=VII|chapter=XII|passage=When the good lieutenant applied himself to the door, he applied himself likewise to the bell; and the '''drawer''' immediately attending, he dispatched him for a file of musqueteers and a surgeon.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1863|author=Sheridan Le Fanu|title=w:The House by the Churchyard|passage=He came down to the Pied Horse Inn, where I was a '''drawer''', at Newmarket, twice.}}
# Someone who taps palm sap for making {{l|en|toddy|id=sap}}.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1927|author=[http://openlibrary.org/authors/OL2416183A F. E. Penny]
|chapter=4|title=[http://openlibrary.org/works/OL16814587W Pulling the Strings]
|passage=A turban and loincloth soaked in blood had been found; also a staff. These properties were known to have belonged to a toddy '''drawer'''. He had disappeared.}}
# {{lb|en|mining|historical}} A [[wagoner]] or person who [[push]]es [[underground]] [[tub]]s.

